---
// Amber on slate only — 5.7:1, passes AA. The same amber on the light sections
// would be 1.9:1, which is why the stat lives on a slate band.
---

<section class="bg-primary text-white" aria-labelledby="outcome-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 text-center sm:py-24">
    <h2 id="outcome-heading" class="sr-only">Results</h2>

    <p class="text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-accent sm:text-6xl">
      10+ hours
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold sm:text-2xl">
      saved per week, typically within the first month
    </p>

    <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/80">
      Not from a new platform. From deleting the copy-paste between two systems
      that were always meant to talk, and the handoffs that quietly sat
      overnight.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
